# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Never commit .env or .env.local.
#
# SERVER-ONLY. `next.config.ts` reads this to build the `/api/:path*` rewrite that keeps the
# browser on one origin. Never rename it to a `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` variable: that would ship the
# backend's address in the client bundle and invite the cross-origin calls the httpOnly
# session cookie cannot survive. See docs/adr/0008-frontend-transport-same-origin-proxy.md.
#
# Must be present at BUILD time as well as at runtime — `next.config.ts` is evaluated by
# `next build`, so a value missing at build silently points the rewrite at localhost:3000.
BACKEND_URL=http://localhost:3000
